8:- Terrain collision (US-053): `terrain_tile_cell` builds one static heightfield per tile, centred on the tile, with absolute heights. `CollisionCellStreamer` loads a cell on activation and requests its unload on deactivation; `cancel_unload` keeps the bodies when a cell reactivates first. Terrain is not a `WorldCell` field, so tile cells are loaded by the caller.
9:- Physics queries and filters (US-053): each body owns an object layer id (`CollisionTable` in `physics_world.cpp`, ids capped at 65535 by `create`). The table holds the filter bit, mask, and motion flag, and `ObjectPairs` reads it. Write it only between steps, like the entity map.
13:- Streamed collision cells (US-053, `collision_cells.cpp`): an unload waits while a dynamic or kinematic body is in the cell's XZ footprint plus margin, at any height. A body falling toward the cell keeps its colliders, so it does not fall through.
1336:- Status call: US-050 meets its CPU acceptance criteria and every gate the tree can run. The renderer needs no rebase (its frame snapshot is camera-relative in double). Physics queries are US-053; the physics adapter is US-052.
